#
# Generic
#

# Module label 'ModuleMediarelayName'
ModuleMediarelayName = MediaRelay
# Module description 'ModuleMediarelayDesc'
ModuleMediarelayDesc = Relays images inserted in product/service descriptions to an OpenMage store
MediaRelayDescription = Relays images inserted in product/service descriptions to an OpenMage store
MediaRelayDescriptionLong = MediaRelay adds an Image button to the CKEditor used on the product and service description fields. Images uploaded or picked from that editor are not stored in Dolibarr: they are relayed to the media library (media/wysiwyg) of an OpenMage/Magento 1 store, through a dedicated admin account, because no OpenMage REST/SOAP API handles image upload without attaching it to a product. Setup: Home > Setup > Modules > MediaRelay (store URL, dedicated admin username and password).

#
# Admin pages
#
MediaRelaySetup = MediaRelay setup
MediaRelaySetupPage = This is the setup page for the MediaRelay module.
MediaRelayAbout = About MediaRelay
MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_URL = OpenMage store URL
MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_URLTooltip = Base URL of the OpenMage/Magento1 store (e.g. https://myshop.com), no trailing slash
MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_USER = OpenMage admin username
MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_USERTooltip = OpenMage admin account dedicated to this integration (System > Permissions > All Users), with access to Content > Design Media
MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_PASSWORD = OpenMage admin password
MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_PASSWORDTooltip = Password of the account above. Automatically encrypted at rest by Dolibarr.
MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_FOLDER = Storage folder
MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_FOLDERTooltip = Subfolder of media/wysiwyg/ to store images in (created automatically if missing). Leave empty to use the media/wysiwyg root.
MEDIARELAY_CLOUDFLARE_ENABLED = Store protected by Cloudflare Access
MEDIARELAY_CLOUDFLARE_ENABLEDTooltip = Enable if the store's /admin/ is protected by Cloudflare Access (Zero Trust): without this, every connection attempt is intercepted by Cloudflare's own login screen before it ever reaches OpenMage.
MEDIARELAY_CLOUDFLARE_CLIENT_ID = Cloudflare Access Client Id
MEDIARELAY_CLOUDFLARE_CLIENT_IDTooltip = Client Id of the Cloudflare Access Service Token dedicated to this integration (Zero Trust > Access > Service Auth).
MEDIARELAY_CLOUDFLARE_CLIENT_SECRET = Cloudflare Access Client Secret
MEDIARELAY_CLOUDFLARE_CLIENT_SECRETTooltip = Client Secret of the Service Token above. Automatically encrypted at rest by Dolibarr.
MediaRelayTestConnectionOK = Connection to OpenMage succeeded (logged in as "%s").
MediaRelayCloudflareAccessStatus = Cloudflare Access:
MediaRelayTestConnectionKOPrefix = Connection failed:
MediaRelayErrorNoFormKey = Invalid OpenMage login page (form_key not found). Check MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_URL, or whether Cloudflare Access protects /admin/ without the module being configured to get past it.
MediaRelayErrorLoginFailed = Login rejected by OpenMage. Check MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_USER and MEDIARELAY_ADMIN_PASSWORD.
MediaRelayErrorRequestFailed = Request to OpenMage failed: %s
MediaRelayErrorHttpCode = Request to %s returned HTTP code %s
MediaRelayErrorContentsFailed = Failed to read the OpenMage folder contents: %s
MediaRelayErrorUploadFailed = Upload to OpenMage failed: %s
MediaRelayErrorUploadFailedPrefix = Upload to OpenMage failed:
MediaRelayErrorUnexpectedUploadResponse = Unexpected response from OpenMage
MediaRelayBrowserTitle = Store images
MediaRelayListNotConfigured = Connection to OpenMage not configured yet (Setup > Modules > MediaRelay).
MediaRelayNoFile = No image found in media/wysiwyg on the store.

